{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 49, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ידאה הנשר", :translit "yida'eh ha-neisher", :gloss "like the eagle swoops"} {:he "בגימ' עשרה", :translit "be-gimatri'ah eser", :gloss "in gematria 10"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ידאה הנשר", :b "עשרה"}], :frame {:text "Sukkah 51b recounts that Alexander the Great marched on Jerusalem; Shimon HaTzaddik went out to meet him and Alexander descended from his chariot and bowed, ultimately treating the Jews favorably. Ba'al HaTurim links the verse's imagery of a swooping eagle to a historical tradition about Alexander arriving in ten days but reaching Jerusalem in one day, reading this into the gematria of 'ידאה הנשר' equaling ten ('עשרה').", :sources ["Sukkah 51b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "ידאה הנשר", :a-value 575, :b "עשרה", :b-value 575, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:40:06.259992640Z", :model "glm-5.2"}